From 9e6df59342b6a1f70dd9e443973ae3c2c6ddeffd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:16:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] camera: frame-rate phase lock, off by default
 (fps_phase_lock)

A sensor frame period is an integer number of lines of the sensor's own
crystal, so a take drifts against the Pi clock that stamps the audio. The
new FramePhaseLock (pure PI servo, 6 us deadband, +/-150 us clamp, whole-
microsecond requests that dither between adjacent line counts) measures
each frame's SensorTimestamp against origin + k/fps on CLOCK_BOOTTIME and
pins FrameDurationLimits {d,d} on the next request, after every other
merge. Referenced to BOOTTIME, not FrameWallClock, because Core's audio is
stamped in BOOTTIME: the audio path is unchanged. Re-arms on fps change,
preview gaps and stalls; counts dropped frames while recording. Setting
fps_phase_lock (persisted, set_fps_phase_lock enabled=true/false), state
field fps_phase_lock, stats line at record stop, APERTAR_PHASE_LOCK_LOG=1
for a per-250-frame trace. Logic ported from Cinemate's phase lock; not
compiled here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
